ARM pairwise widening co-development — 2026-09-07

Host: Apple M4 Pro, aarch64-apple-darwin, 24 GiB installed RAM.
Compiler: rustc 1.98.0 (88d9e12ae), LLVM 22.1.8.
No RUSTFLAGS, CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS, or target-cpu=native.
All heavy commands serialized under nice -n 19, build/Rayon/OMP jobs=4.
The local run-heavy script requires Linux; nice/env caps were used on macOS.
No memory or end-to-end encoder performance result is claimed.

Baseline SVT: 74d92430508f80f6f4faeecef94913977dbf95f2.
Archmage PR #96 baseline: 9981d4f9ad90b0cc57bb244e1b1c16df761bdb20.
https://github.com/imazen/archmage/pull/96
The previous SVT pin cc24398c has identical generated integer APIs to #96 head.
Measured SVT source is the recoverable jj snapshot efea0bca, with the local
archmage pairwise implementation snapshotted as 34251b99. These are LOCAL
revisions, not remote branch names. This change retains the harness and source.
The final from_repr spelling replaces temporary array conversions in 8-byte
remainders; the final binary still matches the baseline NEON ME bodies exactly
(arm_pairwise_codegen_2026-09-07.json).

Method:
- zenbench 0.1.9, randomized/interleaved paired comparisons in one binary.
- Frozen original functions in benches/support/arm_pairwise_reference.rs.
- Identical typed function-pointer call shape for both arms, results consumed
  by zenbench, equality asserted before measurement, default group config.
- 42 groups: SSE/SAD/sum+SSE, 4x4/8x8/16x16/17x9/32x32/64x64/128x128,
  tightly packed and unequal padded strides (w+7, w+14).
- Byte planes use fixed seeded random input; these are DSP kernel measurements,
  not codec quality, content-corpus or fitted calibration measurements.
- SAD is the baseline NeonToken implementation. The encoder's Arm64V2 dotprod
  SAD dispatch arm is untouched; do not attribute this result to that path.

Reproduce: cd rust; just arm-pairwise
The initial command used --help, which zenbench's main! does not interpret.
It ran every group. All 42 pairwise groups finished; the process was stopped
only after it moved into unrelated existing groups. The retained raw text
contains all 42 complete comparisons, not a selected subset.
Raw stdout+stderr: ~/tmp/svt-arm-pairwise-bench-help.log.
Retained paired results: arm_pairwise_2026-09-07.txt.

Result:
No meaningful throughput improvement over handwritten NEON. Larger blocks
mostly have sub-1% paired intervals; the few percent-level differences at
small sizes are not a basis for claiming speedup. Runs include high variance,
which is explicitly printed in the retained output. The useful change is
expressing the existing ARM operations through a portable, exact primitive
without adding instructions: pairwise_widen_add on unsigned bytes/halfwords.
Do not extrapolate this M4 Pro measurement to other ARM microarchitectures.

Codegen:
The final SAD body has 185 identical instructions through its sole return;
sum+SSE has 231. Their total function lengths, including cold panic paths,
are 215 and 261 instructions respectively. Local branch destinations match.
Only cold panic-location metadata is excluded from the hot-body comparison.
Reproduce: python3 tools/perf_profile/arm_pairwise_codegen.py <kernel_tiers-binary>
The archmage gate checks UADDLP/UADALP at all widths, plus x86 and WASM.

Additional experiment (benchmark-only):
Register-only two-row packing: 4-byte rows combined into a u64, 8-byte rows
combined with vcombine_u8, no staging buffer. Four same-binary comparisons
(4x4/8x8, tight/padded) show no useful improvement; do not ship it. See
arm_rowpack_2026-09-07.txt. Before timing, exact scalar/reference comparisons
exercise zero/odd/large heights through 70,000 and unequal strides.
Reproduce: just arm-rowpack

Scope decision:
Keep one new operation name: pairwise_widen_add, u8 -> u16 and u16 -> u32.
Use existing abs_diff, widen_low/high, multiplication and addition around it.
Do not add widening-multiply, square, MAC/MSUB, or signed-pairwise helpers for
this consumer: the measured paths do not require them. PR #96's pre-existing
msub_adjacent is still unused here; removing that PR API is a review decision.

Validation:
- cargo nextest run --workspace -j 4: 2587/2587 passed, 0 skipped.
- tools/regression_spotcheck.sh: 106/106 passed.
- Strict DSP all-target Clippy is NOT green. With --no-deps it reports
  pre-existing doc formatting, drop_non_drop, is_multiple_of, identity_op and
  incompatible_msrv diagnostics. In particular the existing dotprod SAD arm
  uses vdotq_u32/vdot_u32 (stable since 1.98 per Clippy), with declared MSRV 1.89.
  All reported source sites were compared byte-for-byte to baseline 74d92430
  (the entire dotprod function for me_sad.rs); none are introduced here.
  Without --no-deps the existing C-reference build/doc/argument-count/style
  warnings also prevent the strict check. No lint/test expectation was waived.
  DSP diagnostics are retained in arm_pairwise_clippy_2026-09-07.txt.
- Working C reference submodule: 39f909e01 (pre-existing checkout); superproject
  pins 3115c0c1b. The submodule was not modified by this experiment.
- This is a local co-development change, not a merge/release certification.

